ars ago five  years ago folks said let's try to let's  try to knock those barriers down bring  people together start promoting school  choice in an understandable digestible  and in some cases fun way and national  school choice week was born and the goal  of school choice week is really to  empower parents and teachers and  administrators in all different types of  schools and outside of schools to hold  events where they celebrate school  choice where it exists and demand it  where it does not during one week out of  the year and the goal is to start tens  of thousands if not millions of  individual conversations about  educational freedom and then aggregate  all of those stories into an effective  national celebration and we do that  every year in January and we're now as  Lisa said in our fifth year and we do  have five key goals to school choice  week we want to increase public  awareness and demand for school choice  so really letting parents know that they  do have choices where they send their  kids to school and in many play many  places parents don't know the choices  they have so we're trying to let people  know you do have choices in many cases  and then let them know also if you want  more choices like parents have in other  areas stand up have your voices heard  speak out contact your legislators and  demand greater options we want to  encourage the creation and the you know  development of coalition's of school  choice organizations specifically in  states so bringing together these  different sectors and factions whether  it's the open enrollment crowd in public  schools magnet schools charter schools  the voucher proponents the homeschooling  advocates honestly I see I've seen more  fights with in those five or six sectors  than you do between the school choice  crowd and the opposition and we can't  have that type of fighting so we want to  create these coalition's so that when it  comes time to pass crucial legislation  folks are actually getting 